                <pb facs="0425" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg345"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Buck.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that the registration as superficies of titles to perpetual
                    leases is not acceptable to this Government without some authoritative
                    interpretation of the Japanese Government that title under that style is not
                    inferior to that of the perpetual lease; and that, so far as advised, this
                    Government is not prepared to concede that buildings on perpetual leases are
                    subject to taxation not specified in original lease.</p>
                <p>Instructions sent by mail.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
